{"id": "EUVD-2026-76354", "enisaUuid": "39c78fdd-89d2-310b-940b-a49dbc9c9803", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niommu/vt-d: Force requesting ACS when tboot is enabled\n\nCurrently the conditions of requesting ACS in detect_intel_iommu()\ndon't include tboot, leading to a possible misconfiguration with ACS\ndisabled (e.g. due to user opts) while iommu is later forced on by\ntboot_force_iommu().\n\nFix it by checking tboot in detect_intel_iommu().", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:46:57", "baseScore": 9.3, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:C/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/579eb867d3da63f3b5e32f235925e1daa7ec70d0", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aaeb81241e802c86be69394f72d49fde3f861fbb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/45705a6bfdb283f7b3b509010fd617b72f942537", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/87bc611c6c98a41c00feb7b06b0c297dd141a2ae", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/607432b2618b61df81134be0ef2562b8300c1216"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89448", "GHSA-mhhr-wjj6-vjmr"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.14, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00263473-3f60-397e-bca4-c0e5b03d8a7e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5d990b627537e59a3a2f039ff588a4750e9c1a6a <aaeb81241e802c86be69394f72d49fde3f861fbb"}, {"id": "0b7e2b34-b58a-300b-a80c-63d3f1ef7f74", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "192cbccb-959b-396c-afb3-6bf6ab59d2f9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "41d75c99-8d28-3f5a-ad24-f201a0864f3c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.33"}, {"id": "46c3a569-5930-3ca3-b2a1-89bc5a1f0ec4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5d990b627537e59a3a2f039ff588a4750e9c1a6a <60